        <div class="of-project__text-col"><div class="of-project__eyebrow">University City, Philadelphia — University Research Library</div><h2 class="of-project__title">How a Philadelphia University Library Reclaimed Its Reading Room and Protected Its Rare Book Collection</h2><div class="of-project__detail"><span class="of-project__detail-label">Challenge</span><span class="of-project__detail-val">South-facing reading room with intense afternoon glare making study areas unusable; faculty concerned about UV risk to rare book collection housed near windows; elevated energy costs from uncontrolled solar heat gain.</span></div><div class="of-project__detail"><span class="of-project__detail-label">Solution</span><span class="of-project__detail-val">3M Prestige 70 solar control on south-facing reading room glass; UV conservation film on rare book room windows; glare reduced without losing daylight character.</span></div><div class="of-project__detail"><span class="of-project__detail-label">Result</span><span class="of-project__detail-val">Reading room fully usable all afternoon; UV exposure at rare book room reduced to AIC-compliant levels; measurable cooling load reduction; installation completed during semester break without disrupting library operations.</span></div><div class="of-project__detail"><span class="of-project__detail-label">Support Docs</span><span class="of-project__detail-val"><a href="/resources/museum-window-film-3m-prestige-70-solar-control-spec-philadelphia.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">3M Prestige 70 solar control spec</a> and <a href="/resources/library-window-film-llumar-solar-control-spec-philadelphia.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LLumar solar control spec</a>.</span></div><a href="/contact/" class="of-project__cta">Discuss your collection spaces →</a></div>
